=== P2 Feature view 0137 DriveDetailHeader (Windows) ===

Capability AVAILABLE -> not BLOCKED. WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK 2.1.3) + .NET 10 (dotnet 10.0.300) are
installed; the new DriveDetailHeader surface compiles into the WinUI app (TeslaSync.App) and its
UI-thread-free logic is verified by the headless net10.0 test suite below. The web source
(web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/DriveDetailHeader.tsx) is a presentational header (FadeIn
wrapping a back Link, a Route-icon title that is `${startAddress} -> ${endAddress}` or the localized "Drive
Details" fallback, a muted `vehicleName | date | time[ -> end time]` subtitle, and the Replay Link + Share
Button) with no data fetch, so the surface reproduces the Ready branch (route-vs-fallback title +
present-vs-live end time) plus a defensive Loading skeleton. No error/stale/offline state exists in the web
source (those belong to the parent drive-detail page), matching the StatusHeader/QuickNav precedent.

PRE-EXISTING REPAIR (in scope, precedent 0129 QuickNav et al.): TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had again been
left by merge concatenation with multiple <Project> roots + orphaned/unterminated XML comment text (MSB4025),
which blocked the entire solution build/test. Consolidated to a single valid project root: the deduplicated,
path-sorted union of all 464 existing <Compile> links preserved + the new DriveDetailHeader.Model.cs link
(465 total).

